  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 005.8 — the first coming arrival"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Central valley / Garden monuments"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 500"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Senareth, Elyraen, Giant clans, Nephoretti assembly, arriving forces, Aeon Keepers (remote warning)"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: The 500-year Garden era ends during the Festival of First Contact when the sky turns void-black and Anunnaki geometric vessels touch down to harvest the world."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Concludes the 500-year Garden era; leads directly into the Anunnaki orbital entry in chapter 006"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: Major era transition and reveal of the First Coming invasion"
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "The celebration continued into evening as it had for three days—Giants and Nephoretti gathered in the largest valley, surrounded by the monuments they had built together, sharing harmonics and consciousness-touch and the simple joy of existence in community."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Seraneth stood among the assembled thousands, feeling the Prime connection pulse with something that might have been pride."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "The Aeon Keepers could see what had been accomplished, could recognize that their thought-seeds had grown into something worth the sacrifice of entering the Ethereal Realm."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "The sun set in colors that still made their newly-formed eyes ache with beauty."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "Orange and purple and red painting clouds that drifted above pyramids and obelisks, above mountain peaks and forest canopies, above a world that had learned to sing."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Then the colors began to dim."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "Slowly at first—so gradually that most didn't notice immediately."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "But Seraneth, whose consciousness remained perpetually attuned to subtle changes, felt wrongness settle over the valley like cold fog."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "The sunset was fading."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "Not naturally, not with the smooth progression of day yielding to night, but unnaturally."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "As if something was interposing itself between sun and sky, blocking light that should still be reaching them."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "Giants noticed next."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "Their harmonics shifted from celebration to confusion, then to something approaching alarm."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "The temperature dropped—not seasonal cooling, but abrupt chill that made even stone-fleshed beings shiver."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "Darkness descended at wrong speed, from wrong direction."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "Seraneth looked up and felt their entire consciousness recoil from what they saw."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "The sky was going black."
  - line: 55
    type: narration
    text: "Not the natural black of night filled with stars, but void-black."
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Absolute absence of light spreading like infection across the heavens, consuming sunset colors, swallowing clouds, erasing the familiar constellations that had guided them for five centuries."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "And in that spreading darkness, shapes descended."
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "Massive beyond comprehension, geometric forms that hurt to perceive directly, surfaces that reflected no light yet somehow remained visible against the void."
  - line: 60
    type: narration
    text: "Vessels."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "Ships."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "Constructs that shouldn't exist within physical reality yet were manifesting anyway, forcing themselves into dimensions they didn't belong in."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "The celebration died."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "Music ceased."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "Harmonics fell silent as thousands of consciousnesses united in collective recognition of what was arriving."
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "The First Coming."
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "The Aeon Keepers had known."
  - line: 71
    type: narration
    text: "Had always known."
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "That's why they manifested the Nephoretti when they did, why they gave them five hundred years to build something worth defending."
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "Because this moment was inevitable."
  - line: 74
    type: narration
    text: "The darkness."
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "The vessels."
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "The beings who would descend from them carrying purposes that would shatter the Garden like the Pelagor's paradise had been shattered on Tiamat."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "Seraneth felt the Prime connection pulse with grief and determination in equal measure."
  - line: 79
    type: narration
    text: "The Aeon Keepers were sending their final briefing, compressed understanding flooding through dimensions into consciousness barely prepared to receive it:"
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "They come to harvest."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "To enslave."
  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "To reshape this world according to their purposes."
  - line: 84
    type: narration
    text: "You cannot stop them."
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "But you can endure."
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "You can preserve what matters."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "You can ensure that when they eventually leave, enough remains to rebuild."
  - line: 89
    type: narration
    text: "The first vessel touched down on the far side of the island—impact creating tremors that shook pyramids and toppled smaller obelisks."
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "More followed."
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "A rain of geometric impossibility falling from manufactured night, bringing with them cold and fear and the end of everything the Garden had become."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "Giants and Nephoretti stood together in the valley, surrounded by monuments to their cooperation, and watched their world die in darkness and descending shadow."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "The Garden had bloomed for five hundred years."
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "The harvest was beginning."
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 005-the garden blooms"

